AVD-KSV-0106
AVD-KSV-0117

# The eUPF data plane runs as root with the capabilities it needs (NET_ADMIN,
# SYS_ADMIN, SYS_RESOURCE, BPF, PERFMON) to load eBPF programs, mount
# bpffs/debugfs and raise RLIMIT_MEMLOCK - a restricted security context is
# not supported by design.
AVD-KSV-0118

# SYS_ADMIN is what the image entrypoint mounts bpffs and debugfs with; the
# other capabilities are a smaller grant than the privileged container the
# chart ran before, which had every capability and no runtime profile.
AVD-KSV-0005

# The eUPF data plane needs a read-only /sys hostPath mount: the image
# entrypoint mounts bpffs and debugfs under /sys to load the eBPF
# programs. A "disallowed volume type" (hostPath) is by design here.
AVD-KSV-0121
